# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# DOCUMENTED EXCEPTION (issue #1043, maintainer-approved 2026-09-27):
# fixable CVEs, build-stage-only exposure.
#
# The four entries below have a Fixed version and would normally be
# forbidden here. They are excepted because ALL of the amendment's
# conditions hold at once (docs/codebase/security.md):
#   1. Build-stage-only exposure: they exist ONLY in the tailwind-base
#      build stage (node:24-bookworm-slim). Production runtime is
#      python:3.12.14-slim-bookworm (zero fixable HIGH/CRITICAL); the
#      flagged npm-bundled packages (brace-expansion, ip-address, tar)
#      never ship to production.
#   2. No reachable base reduces them today: node 20 (EOL 2026-04-30,
#      frozen) = 29 fixable, node 22 = 8, node 24 = 4.
#   3. Dated expiry: 2026-12-26, same as every other entry.
# They clear with the next upstream node image rebuild: re-pin the
# digest and DELETE these four entries in the same change.

CVE-2026-14257  # 2026-09-27; expires 2026-12-26; EXCEPTION (build-stage-only): fix available (5.0.8) but npm-bundled in tailwind-base only, no production exposure; clears on next node image rebuild
CVE-2026-69152  # 2026-09-27; expires 2026-12-26; EXCEPTION (build-stage-only): fix available (5.0.8) but npm-bundled in tailwind-base only, no production exposure; clears on next node image rebuild
